.TH ASTIR 1 "August 2026" "Astir" "Astir APRS Client"
.SH NAME
astir \- APRS client for amateur radio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B astir
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Astir
listens to a radio or to the internet, decodes what other amateur stations
are transmitting \- positions, weather, messages and telemetry \- and draws
them on a map.
.PP
It is a fork of Xastir with a GTK4 front end, and is a separate program rather
than a newer version of it.  The two install and run side by side and share no
files.  See
.BR FORK.md .
.PP
.B This port cannot transmit.
Beaconing, messaging and digipeating exist in the core and are not reachable
from the user interface.  The per-interface transmit checkbox arms a path that
nothing currently originates traffic on.
.SH OPTIONS
This front end passes its arguments to GTK, and accepts no options of its own
beyond the two below.  Configuration lives in the config file and in the
program's own windows, not on the command line.
.TP
.B \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and build stamp, then exit.  Does not start the program,
read the configuration or require a display, so it still works when the reason
you are asking is that Astir will not start.  Include its output in bug
reports.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Show GTK's option summary.
.SH CONFIGURATION
There is no settings window yet beyond interfaces and map selection.  Your
callsign, home position and every other preference are edited in
.IR ~/.astir/config/astir.cnf ,
with the program closed \- Astir rewrites that file when it exits cleanly, so
edits made while it is running are lost.
.PP
Interfaces are added and started from
.BR "Menu \-> Connections \-> Interfaces" ,
or Ctrl+I.  Astir receives nothing until one is configured.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ASTIR_USER_BASE
Directory to keep
.I .astir
in, instead of the home directory.  Use this to run a second copy, or to test
without risking a working configuration.
.TP
.B ASTIR_DATA_BASE
Where to find maps, symbols, help and styling rules.  Defaults to the installed
data directory.  Astir refuses to start if this points at another program's
data directory.
.TP
.B ASTIR_PERF
Set to 1 to print per-operation timings and geometry counters on exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.astir/config/astir.cnf
Settings, including callsign and position.
.TP
.I ~/.astir/config/map_index.sys
Cached index of available maps.  Delete it, or use
.BR "Menu \-> Maps \-> Rebuild Map Index" ,
after adding map files.
.TP
.I ~/.astir/config/selected_maps.sys
Which maps are drawn.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/astir
Maps, symbols, help text and dbfawk styling rules.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT ", " SIGTERM
Exit cleanly, writing the configuration on the way out.  Ctrl\-C is safe.
.PP
SIGHUP and SIGUSR1 had meanings in the Motif build \- restart, and take a
snapshot \- and are not handled here.
